INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(429800, 0, 4298, 0, 0, 0, 'Plaguelands: The Scarlet Enclave', 'In the far southeastern corner of the Plaguelands, beyond the reach of the blight, the Scarlet Crusade built a haven it called the Scarlet Enclave. Its towns are clean and whole: the farms, mine, mill and stables of Havenshire, the walled town of New Avalon with its hold, chapel and town hall, and ships riding at anchor off the coast. Then a necropolis appeared in the sky. Acherus, the Ebon Hold, has come to rest above the Enclave, and from it the Lich King looses his newest weapon, the death knights, under Highlord Darion Mograine. From the plateau of Death''s Breach below the hold they ride against the Crusade, and beyond the hills to the west stands Light''s Hope Chapel, the Argent Dawn''s stronghold, which the Lich King calls a blemish upon the Plaguelands.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Plaguelands:_The_Scarlet_Enclave (southeastern corner of the Plaguelands, towns pristine and untouched by death, Scarlet holdings); quest 12593 description (Scarlet Crusade, Light''s Hope); quest 12641 description and reward text (forge, town hall, hold, chapel); quests 12670, 12701, 12719, 12756, 12779, 12800, 12801 descriptions and reward texts; page_text 3235 (Unknown Crusader''s Diary: a necropolis appears); quest 12593 description (Light''s Hope stands defiantly against us, a blemish upon these Plaguelands)'),
(429801, 1, 4298, 1, 0, 0, 'Acherus: The Ebon Hold', 'Acherus is a necropolis raised as the citadel of the Lich King''s death knights, and its masters boast that not even Naxxramas could withstand an assault from it. Its design is credited to Obrahiim the Traveler, who also helped conceive Naxxramas. In the Heart of Acherus on the upper floor, Instructor Razuvious measures freshly raised knights, runeforges glow for the etching of blades, and the unworthy hang in chains to be killed. Below lies the Hall of Command, where Highlord Mograine keeps his command post and the masters of blood, frost and unholy teach. Through its great eye the Lich King sees deep into enemy land.', 'quest 12625 description (citadel of death, Naxxramas could not withstand it); page_text 3163 (Compendium of Fallen Heroes: Obrahiim, mastermind behind the creation of Acherus); quests 12593, 12619, 12842, 12848 descriptions (Heart of Acherus, runeforges, unworthy initiates); quest 12849 reward text (Hall of Command, schools of blood, frost, unholy); quest 12626 (Corvus, garrison floor); quest 12636 description (the eye: what the eye sees, the Lich King sees); quests 13165, 13166; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Acherus:_The_Ebon_Hold (Obrahiim, Ebon Blade captured it from Patchwerk); quest 12657 description (command post of Acherus on the first floor); quests 13165 reward and 13166 description (Heart of Acherus is the second floor); creature spawn heights on map 609: Razuvious and the Heart teleporter at z 420, Darion 28444 and the trainers at z 367 to 377'),
(429802, 1, 4298, 2, 0, 0, 'Death''s Breach', 'Death''s Breach is the plateau beneath the floating Ebon Hold, the staging ground for the Scourge''s assault on the Enclave. Scourge gryphons carry knights down from Acherus to a camp of tents, roosts and runeforges, where Prince Valanar drives the assault and Salanar the Horseman, Gothik the Harvester and Orithos the Sky Darkener each claim new blood for their tasks. Here too Olrun the Battlecaller sets initiates to duel one another in Death''s Challenge, a rite said to be born of the Lich King''s victory over Illidan.', 'quest 12670 description (Death''s Breach, staging point, Scourge gryphons); quests 12679, 12680, 12697 givers at Death''s Breach; quest 12733 description (Death''s Challenge, born of the Lich King''s victory over Illidan); quest 12778 description (Lich King stands watch at Death''s Breach); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Death''s_Breach (staging area, later main ground base, Lich King platform); creature spawns grouped by zone_areas.py: Valanar 28377, Gothik 28658, Salanar 28653, Orithos 28647, Olrun 29047, Lich King 29110, Skeletal Gryphon Roost in 4356'),
(429803, 1, 4298, 3, 0, 0, 'Havenshire', 'Havenshire is the working heart of the Enclave, a farming town of fields, pumpkin patches and a lumber mill north of New Avalon''s walls, its people Scarlet peasants and citizens who feed and supply the Crusade. It is the first place the death knights strike. Prince Valanar wants the fleeing villagers killed above all, to plant terror, and the Sky Darkeners loose saronite arrows at anyone running for the safety of New Avalon, while crusaders make their stand to save the horses, mines, lumber and people of the town.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Havenshire (north of New Avalon, constant siege, mill and stables abandoned, citizens fled to New Avalon); quest 12678 description (horses, mines, lumber, citizens; kill the fleeing villagers); quest 12679 description (Sky Darkeners, saronite arrows, fleeing Havenshire for New Avalon); creature_text 28890 (Gothik raising corpses, blasted geists); quest 12716 description and npc_text 13395 (Noth, pumpkin patch, plague cauldron); quest 12714 reward text (Havenshire is ours, a thousand corpses); spawns: Scarlet Peasant, Citizen of Havenshire, Gluttonous Geist, Noth 28919 in 4347 to 4349'),
(429804, 1, 4298, 4, 0, 0, 'Havenshire Stables', 'The Havenshire Stables hold the Crusade''s horses, and so they draw the death knights, who want mounts of their own. Salanar the Horseman sends initiates to steal a steed from under the guards, then has his dark riders slay and raise the beasts as deathchargers in the Realm of Shadows. The stablemaster, Kitrik, has sent more than one horse thief back to the Lich King in pieces. In the stables lies the diary of an unknown crusader, who watched a necropolis darken the bright morning and drew up a map for swimming all the way round the coast to Tirisfal.', 'quest 12680 description (stable full of horses, deranged stable master Kitrik); quest 12687 description (Realm of Shadows, dark rider, deathcharger); creature_text 28683 (Kitrik: how many more of you do I need to send back to the Lich King in pieces); page_text 3235 (Unknown Crusader''s Diary, gameobject 191653 spawned in 4350); spawns: Stable Master Kitrik 28683, Havenshire horses in 4350; page_text 3236 to 3238 (diary entries 15 and 23, swim map); page_text 3237 (Entry 23: the morning is bright, a necropolis)'),
(429805, 1, 4298, 5, 0, 0, 'Havenshire Mine', 'Ore from the Havenshire Mine is carted down to the coast and loaded aboard the Scarlet ships. With the Scourge at its door, the Crusade is trying to strip the mine bare and save what it can, and its miners haul every load they can toward the frigates at anchor off Light''s Point. Gothik the Harvester, grand necromancer of the Lich King, has taken an interest in the place. He has a gift for the Scarlet miners, one he promises will speed up their work: a portable plague spreader.', 'quest 12697 description (strip the Havenshire Mine, load cargo aboard frigates); quest 12698 description, completion and reward text (plague spreader, ghouls, enraged spirits, mines no longer safe); quest 12701 description (mine car near the outhouse); creature_text 28841 (Scarlet Miner: get this down to the ships); spawns: Scarlet Miners, Mine Cars, Inconspicuous Mine Car 190767 in 4365'),
(429806, 1, 4298, 6, 0, 0, 'Light''s Point', 'Light''s Point is the beach east of Havenshire, east of the tower that shares its name, where the Scarlet fleet lies at anchor. With the Scourge loose in Havenshire, the Crusade has thrown every soldier it has outside New Avalon into a blockade here, guarding the frigates while ore from the mine is loaded aboard. Cannons line the shore, and a thousand defenders stand between the Scourge and the ships.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Light''s_Point (beach east of Light''s Point Tower and Havenshire); quest 12697 description (blockade at Light''s Point, frigates docked on the coast); quest 12700 reward text (a thousand soldiers stand between us and their ships); quest 12701 description and reward text (mine car, cannons, entire fleet wiped out in minutes); creature_text 28907 (the Scarlet fleet lies in ruin upon the sundered coast); spawns: Scarlet Fleet Defender, Scarlet Land Cannon in 4353 and 4354'),
(429807, 1, 4298, 7, 0, 0, 'Crypt of Remembrance', 'The Crypt of Remembrance, an old burial vault, stands at the southern edge of Havenshire just north of New Avalon''s wall, bordering the last Scarlet bastion itself. When the death knights fall upon Havenshire, its people run past the vault for the safety of New Avalon''s gate, and the saronite arrows the Sky Darkeners loose at them lie scattered in the farm fields just outside it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Crypt_of_Remembrance (southern Havenshire, north of New Avalon''s wall, forward base); quest 12714 reward text and 12715 description (forward base, Keleseth); npc_text 13419 (Rivendare on the Crusaders); spawns: Keleseth 28911, Rivendare 28910, Fineous 28943, Crypt Guardian 28937 in 4355; quest 12715 description (the crypt borders New Avalon); quest 12679 description (Sky Darkeners, saronite arrows, fleeing Havenshire for New Avalon); gameobject 190691 Saronite Arrow, phaseMask 1 and 2, in Havenshire Farms 4348 just east of the crypt (posarea.py)'),
(429808, 1, 4298, 8, 0, 0, 'New Avalon', 'New Avalon is the last bastion of the Scarlet Crusade in the Enclave, a walled town of orchards, an inn, a forge, a great hold, a chapel and a town hall. Its people were promised safety. As Havenshire''s survivors crowd in, High General Abbendis, with High Abbot Landgren alongside, tells them that only the pure of heart will be allowed to stay, and the inquisitors will turn the rest away. Ghouls hammer at the gates, and frightened citizens beg to know where the last ships are going. Even its inn and forge draw the Scourge''s eye, for Noth the Plaguebringer wants a cauldron and chains for his plague.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/New_Avalon (subzones); quest 12641 description (forge, town hall, hold, chapel); quest 12716 description (the inn and the forge near the gate); creature_text 28548 (Abbendis: only the pure of heart may remain); creature_text 28558 (Landgren); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Brigitte_Abbendis (spoke with Landgren to frightened citizens); quest 12715 description (attacks upon the gates of the last Scarlet bastion, ghouls); creature_text 28941 (we were promised safety, the Scourge are running freely, where are those ships going)'),
(429809, 1, 4298, 9, 0, 0, 'New Avalon Town Hall', 'The town hall is where New Avalon''s officials keep their records and its mayor, Quimby, keeps his seat. In the last days a furious crowd besieges it, shouting that they were promised safety and demanding to know what the Crimson Dawn is and where the ships are bound. Within, councilmen keep to their posts, and the town registry records the births, deaths and comings and goings of the Crusade''s people. Prince Keleseth wants no official left alive.', 'creature_text 28941 (crowd: Quimby, Crimson Dawn, ships, promised safety); quest 12719 description and reward text (assassinate the mayor, registry, three vessels to Northrend, Crimson Dawn); spawns: Mayor Quimby 28945, New Avalon Councilman, New Avalon Registry 190947 in 4346'),
(429810, 1, 4298, 10, 0, 0, 'Scarlet Hold', 'The largest building in New Avalon, Scarlet Hold is the Crusade''s keep in the Enclave, home to its commanders and to High Inquisitor Valroth and his acolytes. Its officers keep a schedule of every patrol route here, and its cells hold the Crusade''s captives, bound in irons. Scarlet Commander Rodrick and his soldiers keep its halls, and its alarms are quick to sound at the first sign of intruders.', 'quest 12724 description (largest building in New Avalon, patrol schedule); quest 12725 description (Koltira dragged in irons to the Scarlet Hold); creature_text 28912 and 29001 (anti-magic barrier, the High Inquisitor comes); quest 12727 description (slay the High Inquisitor and his cronies); spawns: Scarlet Commander Rodrick 29000, High Inquisitor Valroth 29011, Koltira 28912, Patrol Schedule 191084 in 4351'),
(429811, 1, 4298, 11, 0, 0, 'Scarlet Tavern', 'The Scarlet Tavern sits at the southern end of New Avalon, tucked behind the two orchards beside the Chapel of the Crimson Flame. Death knights sent behind the lines to hunt a Scarlet courier have made it their hideout, and Orbaz Bloodbane and Thassarian run their part of the war from its common room, Scarlet corpses strewn across the floor. None of the crusaders they questioned could say when or where the courier would come, so Orbaz plots to steal the patrol schedule from the Scarlet Hold and find out for himself.', 'quest 12723 description (tavern at the southern end, behind the two orchards, adjacent to the chapel; base of operations); quest 12724 description (Scarlet corpses strewn across the floor); quests 12754, 12755 (ambush and disguise planned by Orbaz); quest 12757 description (portal to Acherus); quest 12724 description (we haven''t a clue when or where the courier will show up)'),
(429812, 1, 4298, 12, 0, 0, 'Chapel of the Crimson Flame', 'The Chapel of the Crimson Flame is the Crusade''s church in New Avalon, standing beside the Scarlet Tavern, just west of it, at the town''s southern end, where Scarlet preachers and inquisitors keep watch. It is one of the four Scarlet fortifications in New Avalon, with the forge, the town hall and the hold, that the eye of Acherus was sent to study before the assault. Behind its holy work lies a prison house where the inquisitors hold their captives.', 'quest 12738 description and reward text (raze the chapel, any death knights imprisoned); quest 12739 description (prison house full of Argent Dawn prisoners, most already dead); quest 12751 description (the chapel will be a pile of ashes in a matter of hours); quest 12727 description (executing prisoners at the chapel); spawns: Torch Toss dummies, Scarlet Inquisitor, Plaguefist 29053 and prisoners 29032, 29061 to 29074 in 4352; quest 12723 description (the tavern is adjacent to the chapel); quest 12727 description (they are executing prisoners at the chapel); spawns: Scarlet Inquisitor 29029, Scarlet Preacher 28594 in 4352; quest 12641 description (analyze the forge, town hall, hold and chapel); quest 12738 description (the chapel is due west of the tavern)'),
(429813, 1, 4298, 13, 0, 0, 'Scarlet Overlook', 'A short way east of the Scarlet Tavern lies the Scarlet Overlook, a wide open stretch of road above the way down to King''s Harbor, where the High General keeps the Crusade''s docks. Crusaders swarm along the road and ballistas stand ready beside it, so that anyone on the way down to the harbor passes under a great many watchful eyes.', 'quest 12754 description (courier passes the overlook, roads wide open and swarming with Crusaders, makeshift cover, 200 paces east); creature_text 29076 (Scarlet Courier: what a strange tree); quest 12754 reward text (armies of Hearthglen and Tirisfal marching into a massacre); creature_text 28964 (courier from Hearthglen); spawns: Scarlet Ballista, crusaders in 4360; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/King''s_Harbor (below the Scarlet Overlook); quest 12755 description (Abbendis at King''s Harbor, southeast of the Scarlet Overlook)'),
(429814, 1, 4298, 14, 0, 0, 'King''s Harbor', 'King''s Harbor lies on the bluffs southeast of New Avalon, below the Scarlet Overlook, and its docks belong to the Crusade. Here High General Abbendis stands with High Abbot Landgren and a chosen company guarded by Scarlet champions: a captain and a commander, a bishop, a blacksmith, a foreman, a stable master, a lead cannoneer and even a torturer, while the people of New Avalon beg for a place on the last ship.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/King''s_Harbor (bluffs southeast of New Avalon, below the Scarlet Overlook); quest 12755 description (Abbendis at King''s Harbor); quest 12756 description (turn your armies around, prepare your ships, Scarlet Onslaught); spawns: Abbendis 29077, Landgren 29078, Captain Shely 28549, Commander Jordan 28556, Scarlet Champion 29080 in 4359; creature_text 28941 (I want on that last ship); spawns: Bishop Street, Blacksmith Goodman, Foreman Kaleiki, Lead Cannonneer Zierhut, Stable Master Mercer, Torturer LeCraft in 4359; quest 12755 completion text (you are two hours late)'),
(429815, 1, 4298, 15, 0, 0, 'Browman Mill', 'Browman Mill stands at the edge of the Enclave, just north of Light''s Hope Chapel, reached from Death''s Breach through a cave and the sickly Noxious Glade beyond it. From the mill the land falls away toward the chapel itself, the Argent Dawn''s stronghold, which the Lich King has called a blemish upon the Plaguelands and means to see destroyed once the Crusade has been dealt with.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Browman_Mill (north of Light''s Hope Chapel, Scourge staging ground for the Second Battle for Light''s Hope Chapel); quest 12800 description (Thalanor at the edge of Browman Mill, through the cave into the Noxious Glade); quest 12800 reward text; npc_text 13482 (Darion: here is where I sacrificed everything to free my father); spawns: Thalanor 31082, Darion 29173 in 4364; quest 12593 description (Light''s Hope a blemish upon these Plaguelands); quest 12657 description (when the Crusade has been dealt with, we will finish off the Argent Dawn)'),
(429816, 2, 4298, 1, 0, 0, 'Highlord Darion Mograine', 'Darion Mograine is the son of Alexandros Mograine, the Ashbringer, and a death knight raised in the Lich King''s service. Made Highlord of the death knights of Acherus, he commands the scarlet apocalypse from the Hall of Command, calling on the armies of the Scourge to tear the land asunder. His own words carry the Lich King''s will to the knights, for he hears his master''s voice in his thoughts.', 'quest 13165 description (plunged the Ashbringer into my own heart to free my father''s soul, last memory as a free man); npc_text 13482; creature_text 28444 (the scarlet apocalypse has begun); quest 12657 description (Hall of Command); quest 12706 reward text (since my father wielded...); quest 12801 reward text (join me as a Knight of the Ebon Blade, destroy the Lich King); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darion_Mograine (son of Alexandros, raised by Kel''Thuzad, Highlord, founded the Ebon Blade); quest 12714 description (our existence is tied to his consciousness, Mograine answers an unseen host); creature_text 28444 (tear this land asunder)'),
(429817, 2, 4298, 2, 0, 0, 'The Lich King', 'The Lich King, once Prince Arthas of Lordaeron, rules the Scourge from the Frozen Throne. In the Enclave he comes in person. He greets each new knight in Acherus, bestowing his own anger, cruelty and vengeance along with immortality and the duty of retribution. His judgment on the Scarlet Crusade is death to all, and when the Crusade has been dealt with, he means to finish off the Argent Dawn at Light''s Hope Chapel.', 'quest 12593 description (immortality, force of retribution); quest 12641 reward text (I sense an old enemy, destroyed long ago); quest 12657 description (Death. To. All.); creature_text 29110 (The Light has abandoned you); quest 12779 reward text (helm, Light''s Hope Chapel); creature_text 29183 group 47 and 29175 group 28 (he sent them in to die, knew what lies beneath the chapel); creature_text 28391 (Arthas... my king); quest 13165 reward text; quest 12593 description (all that I am: anger, cruelty, vengeance, I bestow upon you)'),
(429818, 2, 4298, 3, 0, 0, 'Instructor Razuvious', 'Instructor Razuvious, a master of Naxxramas, oversees the making of new death knights in the Heart of Acherus. He judges each body the necromancers raise: a champion is sent to the Lich King, a failure who wakes with emotion and memory intact is disposed of. He sets each initiate to forge a first runeblade, teaches runeforging, and hands over the key that frees an unworthy prisoner to be killed in cold blood, for only then does the endless hunger ease. His word on desertion is posted in the frontline reports: any death knight who deserts will suffer without end, and he will see to it himself.', 'creature_text 28357 (measured, retains emotion and memory, dispose of it); quests 12619, 12842, 12848 descriptions; page_text 3169 (Report from the Frontlines: Eastern Kingdoms); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Acherus:_The_Ebon_Hold (necromancers under Razuvious judged which bodies were worthy); page_text 3239 (ATTENTION: Geists, signed Razuvious)'),
(429819, 2, 4298, 4, 0, 0, 'Prince Valanar', 'Prince Valanar is one of the blood princes of the Scourge, and he leads the death knights'' assault from Death''s Breach. A connoisseur of slaughter, he can smell the crusaders on the wind and openly relishes the feast to come. It is Valanar who teaches the initiates their first lesson in Scourge warfare, terror, ordering that the fleeing villagers of Havenshire die before the soldiers, and from his stage at the Breach he exhorts the knights to leave no survivors.', 'quest 12670 reward text (Valanar sniffs the air, fine cuisine); quest 12678 description (first lesson: TERROR, kill the fleeing villagers); quest 12701 description and reward text (commendation from the Lich King); creature_text 28907 (leave no survivors, speech); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Death''s_Breach (Valanar led the undead, speech from a new stage)'),
(429820, 2, 4298, 5, 0, 0, 'Prince Keleseth', 'Prince Keleseth calls himself the blood lord, ruler of the southeastern reaches of Northrend, and he has come to the Enclave at the Lich King''s request, sweetened by a sea of souls to drink. Prince Valanar calls him his dear brother. From the Crypt of Remembrance he directs the war on New Avalon, refusing to let mindless ghouls do the work alone: its officials must die, to show there is no escape from the Scourge. As with all things the Lich King asks of him, he says, he is happy to oblige.', 'quest 12715 reward text (blood lord, southeastern reaches of Northrend, sea of endless souls); quest 12719 description and reward text; quest 12720 description (persuaders, ornately jeweled box); quest 12715 description (my dear brother, Prince Keleseth)'),
(429821, 2, 4298, 6, 0, 0, 'Koltira Deathweaver', 'Koltira Deathweaver was a high elf of Quel''Thalas, slain when the Scourge invaded his homeland by the human death knight Thassarian and raised to serve the Lich King. The two became brothers in death. Sent behind the lines in New Avalon to hunt a Scarlet courier, Koltira was captured, beaten and dragged in irons to the Scarlet Hold. Found there, he is bitter, calling himself a failure who should have been left to die, since saving the weak defies the dark brotherhood''s covenants.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Koltira_Deathweaver (high elf, slain by Thassarian, brothers in death); quest 12725 description and reward text; creature_text 28912 (ribs broken, anti-magic barrier, I''ll draw their fire); creature_text 28913 (in death we are brothers)'),
(429822, 2, 4298, 7, 0, 0, 'Thassarian', 'Thassarian was a soldier of Lordaeron who followed Prince Arthas to Northrend, was killed there and raised by Arthas as a death knight. In Quel''Thalas he slew the high elf Koltira Deathweaver, who rose as a death knight in turn, and in undeath the two became brothers. At the Scarlet Tavern in New Avalon, when Orbaz blamed the captured Koltira''s weakness and began to hint at his elven blood, Thassarian answered that in life they had been hated enemies, but in death they were brothers, and he would not leave him to the Crusade.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thassarian (Lordaeron soldier, killed in Northrend and raised by Arthas, killed Koltira); creature_text 28913 and 28914 (the Thassarian and Orbaz exchange); quest 12727 reward text (feed this monster''s head to the ghouls); quest 12725 reward text (Koltira: Thassarian, you blasted fool); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thassarian (killed in Northrend by the death knight Falric, then raised by Arthas)'),
(429823, 2, 4298, 8, 0, 0, 'Orbaz Bloodbane', 'Orbaz Bloodbane is a death knight of Acherus who believes only the strong should survive. Sent behind the lines with Thassarian and Koltira, he runs the hunt for the Scarlet courier from the Scarlet Tavern, and plots there with stolen patrol schedules and makeshift cover. He has no sympathy for comrades who fall into enemy hands: when Koltira was taken he said weakness had led to his capture, and began to add scorn for the elf''s blood.', 'npc_text 13444 (we are the chosen ones); creature_text 28914 (his weakness led to his capture, only the strong should survive); creature_text 28913 (What, Orbaz? That he''s a blood elf?); quests 12754, 12755; creature_text 29204 group 71 (Orbaz flees); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Orbaz_Bloodbane (apathetic to captured comrades, fled at Light''s Hope); quest 12723 description (Keleseth sent Orbaz, Thassarian and Koltira); zone_the_scarlet_enclave.cpp Light of Dawn script (Orbaz flees at the end of the fight, before the Lich King appears)'),
(429824, 2, 4298, 9, 0, 0, 'High General Abbendis', 'Brigitte Abbendis is the High General of the Scarlet Crusade, once a paladin of the Silver Hand, who took the rank after a father died shielding the young paladin at Hearthglen. The soldiers say the Light speaks to the High General, who alone chooses who will go and who must stay behind. As the Scourge closes on New Avalon, Abbendis tells its frightened people that only the pure of heart will remain. At King''s Harbor the High General waits impatiently on a courier from Hearthglen, dismayed to hear that the armies of Hearthglen and Tirisfal are marching into a slaughter.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Brigitte_Abbendis (Silver Hand, father died defending Hearthglen shielding her, succeeded him, visions); creature_text 28964 (the Light speaks to the High General; she chooses who may go); creature_text 28548 (only the pure of heart may remain); quest 12755 completion and reward text; quest 12756 description (Scarlet lands are lost, Scarlet Onslaught); quest 12755 completion text (two hours late) and reward text (the armies must not reach New Avalon)'),
(429825, 2, 4298, 10, 0, 0, 'Gothik the Harvester', 'Gothik the Harvester, grand necromancer of the Lich King, came from the frozen heart of Naxxramas to feast on souls, and promptly found himself out of them. At Death''s Breach he receives the knights Valanar sends him with a gift for the Crusade: a portable plague spreader, meant for the Scarlet miners in Havenshire. He has saved a special place for its victims in what he calls his vacuum cleaner of souls.', 'quest 12697 description (grand necromancer of the Lich King) and reward text; quest 12698 description (frozen heart of Naxxramas, all out of souls, plague spreader); creature_text 28890 (rise and fly, blasted geists); creature_text 29112 and 29193 (Noxious Glade deserters: Will it hurt?); spawns: Gothik 29112 and Scarlet Deserter 29193 in 4357; spawns: Gothik 28890 (the corpse-raising Gothik) in Havenshire 4347; quest 12698 completion text (miners do not always become ghouls)'),
(429826, 2, 4298, 11, 0, 0, 'Lord Thorval', 'Lord Thorval, master of the school of blood in the Hall of Command, was once a paladin who left his wife and two daughters at home to hunt the Scourge. He came back to find his village burned and his family dead behind a barred door, killed by the Scarlet Crusade on a rumor of plague. Broken by grief and rage, he was overrun by the very Scourge he had hunted, and swore himself to the Lich King as the blows fell. His memoirs, left for new knights troubled by their past, praise the Scourge for purging the feelings that tormented him. Every mortal story, he writes, ends the same way: in death.', 'page_text 3218 onward (The Memoirs of Lord Thorval, gameobject 191649); quest 12849 reward text (Thorval, headmaster of the school of blood, Hall of Command); npc_text 13173'),
(429827, 3, 4298, 1, 0, 0, 'In Service of the Lich King', 'Every death knight of Acherus begins the same way: raised by necromancers in the Heart of Acherus and measured by Instructor Razuvious. Those found worthy are sent to the Lich King, who gives them immortality and a purpose, to bring doom to the Scarlet Crusade and to Light''s Hope below. Each initiate takes a battle-worn sword from the racks and forges it into a runeblade, learns to etch runes of power upon it, and then is handed a key. Chained nearby are the unworthy, fellow risen who woke with too much of their old selves. One is freed, armed and fought to the death, and the hunger fades.', 'quests 12593, 12619, 12842, 12848, 12636, 12641, 12657 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 28357 (retains emotion and memory); creature_text 29520 (unworthy initiate: I was a soldier of the Light once); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Acherus:_The_Ebon_Hold (necromancers raised bodies Razuvious selected)'),
(429828, 3, 4298, 2, 0, 0, 'The Scarlet Harvest', 'From Death''s Breach the new knights are loosed on Havenshire. Prince Valanar wants terror first: crusaders slain and left for the death march, and above all the fleeing villagers, because killing them is what breaks the hearts of men. Salanar the Horseman has them steal horses from the stables to be remade as deathchargers, Orithos''s Sky Darkeners rain saronite arrows on the roads, and Gothik the Harvester waits with a gift for the miners while the Crusade strips the Havenshire Mine and loads its frigates at Light''s Point.', 'quests 12670, 12678, 12679, 12680, 12687, 12697, 12698, 12700, 12701, 12706 descriptions and reward texts'),
(429829, 3, 4298, 3, 0, 0, 'The Crimson Dawn', 'With New Avalon under siege, Prince Keleseth decides that a few hundred mindless ghouls at the gate will not do. The town''s officials must die to show that none escape the Scourge, so he sends a knight into the town hall to kill Mayor Quimby and bring back the New Avalon registry. Outside the hall a furious crowd is already pounding on the doors, crying that they were promised safety and demanding to know where the last ships are going, and what the Crimson Dawn might be.', 'quests 12719, 12720, 12723, 12724, 12754, 12755, 12756, 12757, 12778 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 28964 (Crimson Dawn is an awakening, the Light speaks to the High General, courier from Hearthglen); creature_text 28941 (crowd at the town hall: promised safety, where are those ships going, Crimson Dawn)'),
(429830, 3, 4298, 4, 0, 0, 'Brothers in Death', 'Orbaz, Thassarian and Koltira were sent behind enemy lines in New Avalon, and breaking through cost them dearly: Koltira Deathweaver was taken, bound in irons and dragged away to the Scarlet Hold, and no one knows whether he still lives. Orbaz would leave him, since in the Scourge only the strong survive, and begins to sneer at the elf''s blood besides. Thassarian, who killed Koltira in life, will not: in death, he says, they are brothers. A knight is sent to tear the hold apart and find him.', 'quests 12725, 12727 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 28912, 28913, 28914; quest 12738 description; creature_text 28913, 28914 (the tavern exchange)'),
(429831, 3, 4298, 5, 0, 0, 'A Special Surprise', 'When Knight Commander Plaguefist''s company tore apart the prison house at the Chapel of the Crimson Flame, looking for death knights the Crusade had taken, they found it full of captured members of the Argent Dawn instead, most of them already dead. Plaguefist saved the few still breathing for the knights to execute, and he picked one out for each of them in particular, a feisty prisoner of the knight''s own race. It was no accident whom they found, and Plaguefist is sure each knight will relish the kill.', 'quests 12739 and race variants 12742 to 12750 (one per race); creature_text 29032 (Malar Bravehorn, Mulgore) and 29061 (Ellen Stanbridge, Elwynn); quest 12739 reward text (You''re Scourge. You''re one of us. Forever); quest 12738 description (if any death knights are imprisoned, Plaguefist will get them out)'),
(429832, 3, 4298, 6, 0, 0, 'The Light of Dawn', 'With the Enclave in ashes, the Lich King gives his last command: Light''s Hope Chapel must fall. His knights pass through the Noxious Glade to Browman Mill, where Scourge Commander Thalanor waits and Darion Mograine is to give the final march orders. The Argent Dawn stands defiant at the chapel, and the knights are promised that this day they ascend into the immortal realm of Scourge heroes. Darion calls the Scourge to rise, and thousands of the dead march on the chapel with the knights of Acherus at their head. The defense of the chapel is told among the tales of the Eastern Plaguelands.', 'quests 12800, 12801 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 29173 (Darion: hear the call of the Highlord, RISE, betrayal, Ebon Blade vow); creature_text 29183 group 47 (I did send them in to die); creature_text 29204 group 71 (Orbaz flees); eastern_plaguelands.json 13933 (chapel side, not repeated); creature_text 29173 groups 26, 43, 68, 69 (we have lost, betrayal, thousands rise, the army marches); zone_the_scarlet_enclave.cpp Light of Dawn script (order: fight ends, Orbaz flees, Darion kneels, later the Lich King appears)'),
(429833, 3, 4298, 7, 0, 0, 'Taking Back Acherus', 'Free of the Lich King, Darion Mograine says the haze has lifted, and he sees as clearly as on the day he drove the Ashbringer into his own heart to free his father''s cursed soul. If his order is to survive in this new world, it needs a home, and its home is still in enemy hands. Each knight is taught to open a death gate and sent back to Acherus, where the first battle of the Knights of the Ebon Blade is already underway. Death to the Scourge, Darion cries.', 'quests 13165, 13166 descriptions and reward texts; quests 13188 and 13189 (Tirion''s letter); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Acherus:_The_Ebon_Hold (Patchwerk, Scourge banners replaced with Ebon Blade banners)'),
(429834, 3, 4298, 8, 2, 0, 'Warchief''s Blessing', 'Death knights who had been heroes of the Horde are sent by Darion Mograine through a portal to Orgrimmar, bearing a letter Tirion Fordring gave on their behalf, for the order needs allies if it is to survive. Their welcome is bitter. On the way to the Warchief, grunts, some of whom lost their families to the Scourge, pelt them with rotten fruit, spit at them and cry murderer, monster and traitorous dog, and some call for a rope or an execution.', 'quest 13189 description and reward text; eastern_plaguelands.json 13918 (Tirion defended an honorable orc); spell_area 58551 (area 0, Horde races 690, from quest 13165 rewarded until 13189 done); creature_text 3296 groups 2 to 5 (rotten fruit, spits, Monster, Murderer, GET A ROPE, traitorous dog, my family was wiped out by the Scourge)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(429800, 1, 0, 255, 'In the end the Enclave burned. Havenshire was put to ruin, the Scarlet fleet sank off Light''s Point and New Avalon was broken street by street, while the Crusade''s High General gave the Scarlet lands up for lost and turned the faithful toward Northrend. The last Scarlet armies to arrive died beneath the necropolis, and the Lich King turned his knights west against Light''s Hope Chapel.', 'quest 12779 reward text (Light''s Hope Chapel); quest 12778 reward text (the ruins of Havenshire and the burning city of New Avalon, the last of the Scarlet armies); quest 12701 reward text (fleet wiped out); quest 12756 description (the Scarlet lands are lost, frozen wastes)'),
(429800, 2, 0, 255, 'At Light''s Hope the Lich King''s hold on his knights was broken. Those who had sacked the Enclave turned against their master, and the necropolis that had carried them here became the home of their own order, the Knights of the Ebon Blade.', 'quest 12801 reward text (the Lich King has loosed his grip, Knight of the Ebon Blade); quests 13165, 13166 descriptions (take back Acherus)'),
(429801, 1, 0, 255, 'The hold did not stay the Lich King''s. After Light''s Hope the knights who broke from him came back through death gates to take it. The Hall of Command fell to them quickly, then the abomination Patchwerk and his horde were cut down in the Heart of Acherus, and the Ebon Hold became the seat of the Knights of the Ebon Blade.', 'quests 13165, 13166 descriptions and reward texts; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Acherus:_The_Ebon_Hold (Ebon Blade captured it from Patchwerk)'),
(429802, 1, 0, 255, 'When Havenshire fell, the plateau became the Scourge''s main base. The Lich King himself came down from Acherus to stand watch over it, and from a platform above the Breach he watched the last Scarlet armies die and taunted them that their Light had abandoned them.', 'quest 12778 description (he stands watch below us, at Death''s Breach); quest 12779 description and reward text; creature_text 29110 (The Light has abandoned you); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Death''s_Breach (later main ground base, Lich King platform); creature 29110 phaseMask 192 (shown from quest 12757 on)'),
(429803, 1, 0, 255, 'Before long Havenshire lay in ruins, a thousand corpses waiting for rebirth. Geists picked over the dead while Gothik the Harvester raised the bodies for the Scourge, cursing the geists who got to them first, and Noth the Plaguebringer set a plague cauldron in the pumpkin patch to rot the land.', 'quest 12714 reward text (Havenshire is ours, a thousand corpses); creature_text 28890 (Gothik raising corpses, blasted geists); quest 12716 description and npc_text 13395 (Noth, pumpkin patch, plague cauldron); creature 28890 and 28919 phaseMask 4 (spell_area 52597/52598, after quest 12706)'),
(429804, 1, 0, 255, 'Its earlier pages read differently once the town registry has given up its secret. The author had come to fear that Abbendis was splitting the Crusade to sail north against the Lich King''s own citadel with only the most faithful, leaving New Avalon and Tyr''s Hand to burn.', 'page_text 3236 (Entry 15: a schism, attack the Lich King''s citadel with a fraction of the most faithful, leave New Avalon and Tyr''s Hand to burn); quest 12719 reward text (three vessels sailing to Northrend)'),
(429805, 1, 0, 255, 'The gift was turned loose among the miners. Some rose as ghouls to follow their killers, others as raging spirits, and the panic emptied the tunnels and sent the Crusade scrambling for its ships, their backs open to the Scourge.', 'quest 12698 description, completion and reward text (ghouls, enraged spirits, mines no longer safe, retreating with their backs open)'),
(429805, 2, 0, 255, 'The Scourge had one more use for the mine. Its agents left a mine car near the outhouse, so that an unwitting Scarlet miner would wheel a hidden death knight straight down to the docks and behind the Crusade''s blockade.', 'quest 12701 description (mine car near the outhouse, placed safely behind enemy lines)'),
(429806, 1, 0, 255, 'It did not matter. A death knight smuggled behind the blockade in a mine car got aboard a ship and turned its own cannons on the beach, and in minutes the entire Scarlet fleet was wiped out, its ruins left burning along the sundered coast.', 'quest 12701 description and reward text (mine car, cannons, entire fleet wiped out in minutes); creature_text 28907 (the Scarlet fleet lies in ruin upon the sundered coast)'),
(429807, 1, 0, 255, 'Once Havenshire fell, the Scourge moved in behind its ghouls and took the crypt as its forward base for the assault on New Avalon. Prince Keleseth held court there with Baron Rivendare of Stratholme, crypt guardians kept watch, and a quartermaster named Fineous traded with knights returning from the front. Rivendare, who judged the crusaders a uniquely witless lot, mused that a mere mention of the Light would send them rushing headlong into any fight.', 'quest 12714 reward text (our forces have moved in behind the ghouls and taken the Crypt of Remembrance); quest 12715 description (new forward base, Keleseth); npc_text 13419 (Rivendare on the Crusaders); spawns: Keleseth 28911, Rivendare 28910, Fineous 28943, Crypt Guardian 28937 in 4355, all phaseMask 4 (after quest 12706)'),
(429808, 1, 0, 255, 'The walls did not hold. The dead knights followed the ghouls in, the Scourge ran freely through the streets, and the High General gave the town up for lost. When the last Scarlet armies came to save it, New Avalon was already burning.', 'creature_text 28941 (the Scourge are running freely through the streets); quest 12756 description (New Avalon and Havenshire are overrun); quest 12778 description and reward text (armies arrive to see their enclave in flames, the burning city of New Avalon)'),
(429809, 1, 0, 255, 'Keleseth sent a death knight to kill the mayor and seize the registry. Among its ledgers of births and deaths were the movements of three vessels already sent abroad, bound for Northrend, and beside their course the words Crimson Dawn.', 'quest 12719 description and reward text (assassinate the mayor, registry, three vessels to Northrend, Crimson Dawn)'),
(429810, 1, 0, 255, 'Among the captives is a death knight. Koltira Deathweaver, taken as his band broke through the Scarlet lines, was bound in irons and dragged here, and those he left behind at the Scarlet Tavern do not know whether he is dead or alive.', 'quest 12725 description (Koltira bound in irons and dragged to the Scarlet Hold)'),
(429810, 2, 0, 255, 'A rescuer broke in and found him. Badly hurt, Koltira raised an anti-magic barrier and held it while High Inquisitor Valroth came down with his acolytes to deal with the intruders himself. The High Inquisitor of New Avalon did not leave the hold alive.', 'creature_text 28912 (anti-magic barrier, the High Inquisitor comes); quest 12727 description and reward text'),
(429811, 1, 0, 255, 'The plot came home to the tavern. A knight returned wearing the dead courier''s clothes and bearing the High General''s own journal, and Orbaz laughed at it as a child''s coloring book: the faithful, he said, were sailing to their deaths. Then he opened a portal from the tavern straight back to Acherus.', 'quest 12756 completion and reward text (Orbaz laughs, coloring book, they sail to their deaths); quest 12757 description (portal to Acherus)'),
(429812, 1, 0, 255, 'Word came out of the Scarlet Hold with Koltira Deathweaver''s rescuer: the Crusade was executing prisoners at the chapel. Thassarian would see Koltira''s cry for vengeance heard: Knight Commander Plaguefist and a company of death knights were already riding to raze the chapel and free any of their own held there.', 'quest 12727 description (tell Thassarian they are executing prisoners at the chapel); quest 12738 description (cry for vengeance, Plaguefist and a company of death knights, free any death knights imprisoned; offered at the 12727 turn-in)'),
(429812, 2, 0, 255, 'When they tore the chapel apart, they found none of their own. The Crusade had been busy: the prison house was full of Argent Dawn prisoners instead, most of them already dead.', 'quest 12738 reward text (we did not find any of our brothers); quests 12739, 12742 to 12750 descriptions (prison house full of Argent Dawn prisoners, most already dead)'),
(429812, 3, 0, 255, 'The few still breathing were left for death knights to execute, and the chapel was put to the torch. Koltira''s cry for vengeance had been answered, and within hours the Chapel of the Crimson Flame would be a pile of ash.', 'quests 12739, 12742 to 12750 reward text; quest 12751 description (cry for vengeance answered, a pile of ashes in a matter of hours)'),
(429813, 1, 0, 255, 'A courier from Hearthglen was due to pass here with word for the High General. Orbaz Bloodbane hid a death knight at the overlook under makeshift cover, disguised as a tree. When the curious courier stopped to inspect it, the knight cut him down and took his message and his clothes. The message revealed that the armies of Hearthglen and Tirisfal were marching into a massacre.', 'quest 12754 description and reward text; creature_text 29076 (what a strange tree); quest 12754 description (the courier is scheduled to pass by the overlook)'),
(429814, 1, 0, 255, 'The High General was waiting on a courier from Hearthglen. A disguised death knight brought the stolen message instead and carried away the final orders: the Scarlet lands were lost, so the armies must turn around and make ready to sail for the frozen wastes. The faithful of the Crimson Dawn were bound for Northrend, no longer the Scarlet Crusade but the Scarlet Onslaught.', 'quest 12755 description and reward text; quest 12756 description (turn your armies around, prepare your ships, Scarlet Onslaught); quest 12755 completion text (you are two hours late)'),
(429815, 1, 0, 255, 'With the Scarlet Enclave destroyed, the Lich King made the mill the staging ground for his last blow. Scourge Commander Thalanor waited there, and Highlord Darion Mograine gathered the death knights of Acherus and the risen armies for the march on the chapel.', 'quest 12800 description and reward text; creature 29173 and 31082 phaseMask 128 (after quest 12779)'),
(429815, 2, 0, 255, 'Waiting at the mill with his army, Darion said the chapel below was where he had once sacrificed everything to free his father. Now, he said, he came to destroy it.', 'npc_text 13482 and 13485 (gossip menu 9795 of Darion 29173 at Browman Mill, no conditions)'),
(429816, 1, 0, 255, 'Yet something of the old Darion lingered. Reading of the Scarlet fleet''s destruction, he marveled that he had not seen such power in years, not since his father wielded... and there he shook his head and let the thought go.', 'quest 12706 reward text (since my father wielded..., shakes his head)'),
(429816, 2, 0, 255, 'At Browman Mill, where the army gathered for the march, Darion looked toward Light''s Hope Chapel and said it was where he had sacrificed everything to free his father. Now, he said, he came to destroy it.', 'npc_text 13482 and 13485 (gossip menu 9795 of Darion 29173 at Browman Mill)'),
(429816, 3, 0, 255, 'After Light''s Hope he freed himself and his knights. The haze had lifted, he said, and he saw as clearly as on the day he drove the Ashbringer into his own heart to free his father''s cursed soul, his last memory as a free man. He founded the Knights of the Ebon Blade and swore to destroy the Lich King.', 'quest 12801 reward text (join me as a Knight of the Ebon Blade, destroy the Lich King); quest 13165 description (plunged the Ashbringer into my own heart to free my father''s cursed soul, last memory as a free man)'),
(429817, 1, 0, 255, 'Through the eye of Acherus he studied New Avalon''s defenses and found more than he expected. He sensed an old enemy there, one he had thought destroyed long ago, and resolved to send the full might of the Scourge before the Crusade could ready itself.', 'quest 12641 reward text (I sense an old enemy, destroyed long ago; the full might of the Scourge)'),
(429817, 2, 0, 255, 'When the Enclave burned, he came down to Death''s Breach and taunted the last crusaders that their Light had abandoned them. Then he set a helm upon each champion''s head and turned their eyes west, to Light''s Hope Chapel.', 'creature_text 29110 (The Light has abandoned you); quest 12779 reward text (helm, Light''s Hope Chapel)'),
(429817, 3, 0, 255, 'He had sent them to die. Tirion Fordring told Darion his master knew what lay beneath the chapel, and when the Lich King came to Light''s Hope himself, he admitted it: their lives were worth nothing to him. Darion Mograine turned on him, and struck by the Ashbringer in Tirion''s hands, the Lich King vanished from the field, swearing their next meeting would not be on holy ground.', 'creature_text 29175 group 28 (your master knows what lies beneath the chapel, he has sent you to meet your doom); creature_text 29183 group 47 (you were right, Fordring, I did send them in to die) and group 58 (not on holy ground); creature_text 29173 group 43 (betrayal) and 81 (throws the Ashbringer to Tirion), 29175 group 83 (Tirion strikes the Lich King); zone_the_scarlet_enclave.cpp Light of Dawn outro (the Lich King leaves by an exit teleport, scene 47)'),
(429819, 1, 0, 255, 'It was Valanar who sent a knight into the mine car that destroyed the Scarlet fleet, and he greeted the news with delight: the entire fleet wiped out in minutes. He expected a commendation from the Lich King for that victory.', 'quest 12701 description and reward text (commendation from the Lich King)'),
(429820, 1, 0, 255, 'He had the mayor murdered for the town registry, and from its pages worked out that Scarlet ships were sailing for Northrend, beside them the words Crimson Dawn. To learn why, he handed out his jeweled persuaders and set his knights to torturing the truth out of the crusaders.', 'quest 12719 description and reward text; quest 12720 description (persuaders, ornately jeweled box)'),
(429821, 1, 0, 255, 'Yet broken ribs and all, he raised an anti-magic barrier to shield his rescuer while the High Inquisitor came for them, and when Valroth fell he stayed behind to draw the Crusade''s fire. Thassarian insisted the walls could not hold him.', 'creature_text 28912 (ribs broken, anti-magic barrier, I''ll draw their fire); quest 12727 reward text (those walls can''t hold him)'),
(429822, 1, 0, 255, 'Koltira, rescued, called him a blasted fool for breaking the dark brotherhood''s covenants. When High Inquisitor Valroth''s head came back to him, Thassarian promised it to the ghouls and tossed it aside, certain that his brother had made it out.', 'quest 12725 reward text (Thassarian, you blasted fool); quest 12727 reward text (feed this monster''s head to the ghouls, those walls can''t hold him)'),
(429823, 1, 0, 255, 'The scheme that fooled the High General was his: an ambush at the overlook, a dead man''s clothes, a dark disguise. When the courier''s journal came back to him, Orbaz laughed at it as a child''s coloring book.', 'quests 12754, 12755 descriptions; quest 12756 completion and reward text'),
(429823, 2, 0, 255, 'At Light''s Hope Chapel, when a holy light broke over the field and the fighting stopped, Orbaz did not wait to see what would follow. He fled before Darion Mograine had even fallen to his knees.', 'creature_text 29204 group 71 (Orbaz flees); zone_the_scarlet_enclave.cpp Light of Dawn script (Orbaz flees at EVENT_FINISH_FIGHT_2, Darion kneels later at EVENT_OUTRO_SCENE_1)'),
(429824, 1, 0, 255, 'Deceived by a disguised death knight, Abbendis declared the Scarlet lands lost, sent word for the armies of Hearthglen and Tirisfal to turn around and make for the frozen wastes, and proclaimed the end of the Scarlet Crusade and the birth of the Scarlet Onslaught.', 'quest 12756 description (Scarlet lands are lost, Scarlet Onslaught)'),
(429825, 1, 0, 255, 'The plague spreader did its work. Turned loose among the Scarlet miners, it raised some as ghouls to follow their killers and others as raging spirits, for miners, Gothik allowed, do not always become ghouls. The panic emptied the mine and sent the Crusade running for its ships.', 'quest 12698 reward text (the mines are no longer safe); quest 12698 completion text (miners do not always become ghouls)'),
(429825, 2, 0, 255, 'When Havenshire fell he went among its dead, raising the Scarlet fallen as ghouls and their slain gryphons to fly again for the Scourge, and cursing the gluttonous geists who chewed the bodies before he could get to them.', 'creature_text 28890 (rise and fly, blasted geists); spawns: Gothik 28890 in Havenshire 4347, phaseMask 4; zone_the_scarlet_enclave.cpp Gothik script (dead Scarlet Gryphon 28893 raised with the gryphon spell, other Scarlet corpses as ghouls)'),
(429825, 3, 0, 255, 'Later, in the Noxious Glade, he experimented on captured Scarlet deserters floating in vats of slime, assuring one who asked whether it would hurt that it would, immensely, and would probably knock him out.', 'creature_text 29112 and 29193 (Noxious Glade deserters: Will it hurt?); spawns: Gothik 29112 and Scarlet Deserter 29193 in 4357, phaseMask 128 (after 12779)'),
(429827, 1, 0, 255, 'Then the Lich King lent the initiate the eye of Acherus, and through its probe the knight studied the forge, town hall, hold and chapel of New Avalon. The Crusade was preparing for battle, as expected, but the Lich King sensed something more: an old enemy, one he had destroyed long ago.', 'quests 12636, 12641 descriptions and reward texts'),
(429827, 2, 0, 255, 'His judgment followed, carried to Highlord Mograine in the Hall of Command: Death. To. All. When the Crusade had been dealt with, the Argent Dawn would follow. The horns of war sounded across the land, and the march on New Avalon began.', 'quest 12657 description and reward text'),
(429828, 1, 0, 255, 'Gothik''s plague spreader turned the miners into ghouls and raging spirits. In the chaos the Crusade pulled back to its ships at Light''s Point, and only New Avalon and the blockade on the coast still stood against the Scourge.', 'quest 12698 reward text; quest 12700 description (only the Scarlet forces at New Avalon and Light''s Point challenge us)'),
(429828, 2, 0, 255, 'Valanar seized the moment. A knight hidden in a mine car was carried behind the blockade, turned the ships'' cannons on the thousand defenders, and the whole fleet was destroyed in minutes.', 'quests 12700, 12701 descriptions and reward texts'),
(429828, 3, 0, 255, 'Darion Mograine, reading Valanar''s report of the victory at Death''s Breach, could only wonder at it. Such power, he said, he had not seen in years, not since his father wielded... and he shook his head and let the thought go.', 'quest 12706 reward text'),
(429829, 1, 0, 255, 'The registry gave up its secret. Three Scarlet ships had already sailed for Northrend, and beside their course stood the words Crimson Dawn. Keleseth could scarcely believe it, and handed out his jeweled persuaders to have the truth tortured out of the crusaders.', 'quest 12719 reward text; quest 12720 description'),
(429829, 2, 0, 255, 'Prisoners spoke of an awakening, of a Light that speaks to the High General, who alone chooses who goes and who stays. One, at the last, gave up that a courier was coming from Hearthglen.', 'creature_text 28964 (Crimson Dawn is an awakening, the Light speaks to the High General, courier from Hearthglen); quest 12720 reward text'),
(429829, 3, 0, 255, 'Orbaz Bloodbane laid the trap. A knight waited in hiding at the Scarlet Overlook and killed the courier, and his message told that the armies of Hearthglen and Tirisfal were marching into a massacre.', 'quests 12723, 12724, 12754 descriptions and reward texts'),
(429829, 4, 0, 255, 'Wearing the courier''s clothes and face, the knight carried the message to Abbendis at King''s Harbor. Believing the courier true, the High General gave up the Enclave as lost, sent word for the approaching armies to turn for the frozen wastes, and handed over a journal. The Crusade was no more; the Scarlet Onslaught was born.', 'quests 12755, 12756 descriptions and reward texts'),
(429829, 5, 0, 255, 'Orbaz laughed at the journal, sure the faithful were sailing to their deaths, and sent it on to Acherus. Mograine turned to the armies already on the march: the Scourge would ravage them and raise their dead as its own.', 'quest 12756 reward text; quest 12757 reward text (we will ravage these approaching armies and raise the dead as our own); quest 12778 description (the trap has been sprung)'),
(429830, 1, 0, 255, 'Koltira was found, half broken, and cursed the rescue as a breach of the dark brotherhood''s covenants: now two of them might die. The alarms had sounded and the High Inquisitor was coming. If his rescuer lived, Koltira said, Thassarian should know the Crusade was executing prisoners at the chapel.', 'quest 12725 reward text; quest 12727 description'),
(429830, 2, 0, 255, 'Koltira shielded his rescuer inside an anti-magic barrier while High Inquisitor Valroth and his acolytes came for them. Valroth fell, and Koltira stayed behind to draw the Crusade''s fire. Thassarian, handed the inquisitor''s head, insisted his brother would find his way out, and turned to payback.', 'creature_text 28912 (anti-magic barrier, I''ll draw their fire); quest 12727 reward text'),
(429831, 1, 0, 255, 'The prisoner knew the knight: a champion of their own people, from their own homeland, now wearing the Scourge''s colors. Bleeding and chained, the prisoner begged the knight to remember where they were born and the splendor of life, to fight the Lich King''s grip and be a hero again. There was no time. The prisoner asked for a quick end before they were both killed, and the knight gave it. Plaguefist was pleased: the knight was not one of them anymore. They were Scourge, forever.', 'creature_text 29032 (Malar Bravehorn, Mulgore) and 29061 (Ellen Stanbridge, Elwynn); quest 12739 reward text (You''re Scourge. You''re one of us. Forever)'),
(429832, 1, 0, 255, 'The battle ended when a holy light broke over the field and the fighting stopped. Orbaz Bloodbane fled, and Darion fell to his knees: they had lost. Then their master came and admitted he had sent them there to die. Darion turned on him, crying betrayal, and threw the Ashbringer to Tirion Fordring, in whose hands it drove the Lich King from the field. Afterward Darion called his knights to Acherus as Knights of the Ebon Blade, monsters with no atonement left but amends paid in death, sworn to destroy the Lich King.', 'creature_text 29173 groups 26, 43, 81 (we have lost, betrayal, throws the Ashbringer to Tirion); creature_text 29183 group 47 (I did send them in to die); creature_text 29204 group 71 (Orbaz flees); zone_the_scarlet_enclave.cpp Light of Dawn script (Orbaz flees at EVENT_FINISH_FIGHT_2, Darion kneels at EVENT_OUTRO_SCENE_1, the Lich King appears at EVENT_OUTRO_SCENE_20); quest 12801 reward text'),
(429833, 1, 0, 255, 'The Lich King had returned to Northrend, wounded by the Ashbringer, and the Hall of Command was secured quickly. But he had left a parting gift in the Heart of Acherus: the stitched horror Patchwerk and a horde of abominations.', 'quest 13165 reward text; quest 13166 description'),
(429833, 2, 0, 255, 'Knights fought together to cut them down, the Scourge banners came down, and the Ebon Hold belonged to the Ebon Blade, its rebuilding begun anew. One last task remained: each knight would carry Tirion Fordring''s letter to the leaders of their old people.', 'quest 13166 reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Acherus:_The_Ebon_Hold (Patchwerk, Scourge banners replaced with Ebon Blade banners); quests 13188 and 13189 descriptions (Tirion''s letter)'),
(429834, 1, 0, 255, 'Thrall read the letter and remembered: Tirion was the paladin who had given up everything to save the orc Eitrigg from execution, and the warchief had known only one other human willing to make such a sacrifice. Blinking back a tear, he spoke Taretha''s name. For Tirion and for Eitrigg, he accepted the knights back into the Horde and their order as allies. Blood and honor, he declared.', 'quest 13189 reward text');
